WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:06.480
In previous videos, we talked about different&nbsp;
solutions we have for living in Project Kamp.

00:00:06.875 --> 00:00:10.143
Some people come with their own vans 
and others&nbsp;bring just tents...

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:17.266
In this video, we're going to prototype and install a custom tent,
on top of a&nbsp;deck in a different area of the land.

00:00:17.266 --> 00:00:19.698
Welcome to a new Project Kamp update!

00:00:21.672 --> 00:00:23.697
So, we want to make our&nbsp;tents for several reasons...

00:00:24.797 --> 00:00:29.139
An important one is to provide a solution for us,
that can be replicated&nbsp;by others.

00:00:29.139 --> 00:00:32.640
So we will share the design drawings,
and information on how to make it.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.066
Now, let me tell&nbsp;you about what kind of tent we are going to build.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:41.299
Camping tents are usually designed for&nbsp;short stances.

00:00:41.299 --> 00:00:44.886
For being carried easily in a light weight...

00:00:44.886 --> 00:00:47.262
Easy to assemble and to disassemble.

00:00:48.052 --> 00:00:50.300
Usually made out of plastic too...

00:00:50.779 --> 00:00:55.005
They are low for the wind, and for easy transportation too...

00:00:55.005 --> 00:00:59.054
So, that's something that really doesn't fit our needs...

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:03.005
And, after some researching in the market 
and what&nbsp;is out there...

00:01:03.005 --> 00:01:05.618
We came up with the idea to design our own tent.

00:01:05.844 --> 00:01:10.846
So, we want to design a tent for&nbsp;one person,
where you can stand to be more comfy.

00:01:11.301 --> 00:01:16.691
We also want to use other materials,
because it&nbsp;doesn't need to be carried around often.

00:01:16.691 --> 00:01:22.320
So, for us, it's just setting it up at the beginning of the&nbsp;Season,
putting it down at the end of the season.

00:01:23.363 --> 00:01:28.486
We also want to make it not too big, 
in&nbsp;order to put it on top of a wooden platform.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.850
To have it level, and increase the comfort inside.

00:01:32.132 --> 00:01:35.202
This also would help us to keep it for a longer time.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:39.101
So, the materials are not really touching the&nbsp;soil or the ground...

00:01:39.101 --> 00:01:42.408
Hopefully, this tent lasts way more years!

00:01:43.423 --> 00:01:46.893
So, we have to choose where&nbsp;to place the tent on our land...

00:01:46.893 --> 00:01:50.537
We decided to go away from Basekamp,
to set it down&nbsp;in the field.

00:01:50.932 --> 00:01:52.561
Next to the creek, and the yoga deck.

00:01:52.561 --> 00:01:56.711
It's more a quiet and relaxed&nbsp;space,
where you can hear nature sounds.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.062
Away from noises, and the busy setup in Basekamp!

00:02:01.513 --> 00:02:04.969
To build the deck, we went searching for our wood 
from the local sawmill...

00:02:04.969 --> 00:02:08.251
And we are taking&nbsp;it to the Kamp with our brand new pickup!

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:12.334
We are using red cedar with no treatment.

00:02:12.334 --> 00:02:16.889
Because in the winter, our beloved roundabout sign 
did very well and didn't get moldy.

00:02:16.889 --> 00:02:18.083
So, we got the wood!

00:02:18.083 --> 00:02:21.497
Now it's ready to be handed to Eemeli!

00:02:21.497 --> 00:02:23.514
To be transforming our NEW tent decks!

00:02:25.065 --> 00:02:25.570
Let's do it!

00:02:25.570 --> 00:02:26.573
- Let's go!

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.526
Hi, I'm Eemeli!

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:34.680
I came to Project Kamp to work&nbsp;in both design and building.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:41.640
That's also what I've been working on in Finland.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:50.100
So, it's nice to continue with&nbsp;it in really different settings.

00:02:50.577 --> 00:02:53.100
And to get a little more practice on these skills.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:57.540
So, let's see how it goes!

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:49.599
Okay, now the wood is ready.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.720
So next, we are gonna go and see the place.

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:41.744
Okay, now we are here in the bottom of&nbsp;the field.

00:04:41.744 --> 00:04:47.806
And the first thing is to get rid of 
the grass, and level the ground.

00:05:27.833 --> 00:05:30.171
I found this metal wire...

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:35.301
Seems like&nbsp;some kind of fence has been here...

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:37.947
I don't really know...

00:05:38.398 --> 00:05:42.271
I think I will&nbsp;leave it for now and continue digging.

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:31.707
The ground work is now complete!

00:06:31.707 --> 00:06:34.440
So, next we need to find a few rocks...

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:55.643
Okay, now we have all the rocks that we need...

00:06:57.313 --> 00:07:00.405
So, now we can finally bring all the wood here!

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:29.286
The deck is now complete!

00:09:29.286 --> 00:09:30.873
I think it looks nice!

00:09:32.424 --> 00:09:37.552
I still want to do some&nbsp;grass cutting,
to clean out the area a bit.

00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:59.292
Okay, the deck is ready.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.600
The wood is not&nbsp;treated,
because we will use it as a test.

00:10:03.108 --> 00:10:05.685
We want to compare it with another&nbsp;deck close by...

00:10:05.685 --> 00:10:08.003
Made with the same wood, but with industrial treatment.

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:10.627
Let's&nbsp;see how they behave in the long run!

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:32.054
Next, we need the tent to be created.

00:10:32.364 --> 00:10:33.975
We asked&nbsp;Kaegh and Eva for help.

00:10:34.426 --> 00:10:38.229
They are very skilled, and also happen to be 
good friends that live close by.

00:10:38.229 --> 00:10:40.950
They&nbsp;have a really nice camping side in the mountains!

00:10:41.176 --> 00:10:45.023
Where they have installed a yurt, 
and a big dome made by themselves.

00:10:45.023 --> 00:10:49.666
So we thought it's a good idea that they take care of 
building the canvas,&nbsp;and the tent frame.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.934
Let's see how they work on it!

00:10:54.761 --> 00:10:58.880
 

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:32.640
 

00:14:47.947 --> 00:14:50.000
We are now waiting for Kaegh and Eva!

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:52.867
They're coming to bring the tent to the camp,
and build it on the location.

00:14:57.191 --> 00:14:58.561
- Hello!

00:15:03.660 --> 00:15:04.823
So, we made it!

00:15:04.964 --> 00:15:06.077
Nice!

00:15:06.077 --> 00:15:07.934
Now, we have all of&nbsp;the team in the Kamp!

00:15:07.934 --> 00:15:09.753
Eemeli built the deck...

00:15:09.753 --> 00:15:11.101
Eva made the canvas...

00:15:11.101 --> 00:15:12.664
Kaegh made the frame...

00:15:12.664 --> 00:15:17.280
Now we have all the pieces, and we need to put them together,&nbsp;
to build our tent on top of the deck!

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:17.307
Would it be cool later to mark the screws,
that we need to unscrew to disassemble it?

00:16:17.307 --> 00:16:21.240
- Yeah, I was going to change the screws,
that you need to unscrew to bolts.

00:16:56.173 --> 00:16:58.003
Where you do put in the bolts?

00:16:58.538 --> 00:17:02.813
- So, we wanted to&nbsp;make it as easy 
as possible to disassemble...

00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:08.704
So we're trying to have the bolts for the&nbsp;
temporary connections...

00:17:08.704 --> 00:17:12.771
And then, everything else is either screwed or glued together...

00:17:13.363 --> 00:17:16.848
So, then you&nbsp;only need to take apart the bolts to take it down.

00:17:31.511 --> 00:17:32.842
Hear that, Eva?

00:17:32.842 --> 00:17:33.400
- Huh?

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:35.226
You did a super nice job!

00:17:35.226 --> 00:17:35.726
- Aw, thank you!

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:15.499
So as you can see here in the wood,
we drilled these pieces in.

00:18:15.499 --> 00:18:19.031
And this is then the other side of the 
buttons that are on&nbsp;the fabric.

00:18:19.031 --> 00:18:21.359
So, the fabric is really easy, just like a button.

00:18:21.359 --> 00:18:26.160
You can just press it in and&nbsp;it's connected to the wood.

00:20:36.360 --> 00:20:38.147
Okay, so, this is the tent!

00:20:38.534 --> 00:20:40.751
We've set it up, and it's basically done!

00:20:41.005 --> 00:20:44.960
I sewed some strings here,
so you can just tie it...

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:49.064
This is one piece...

00:20:49.677 --> 00:20:52.781
I did them separately,
 but&nbsp;then I sewed them together here.

00:20:52.781 --> 00:20:55.401
And as you can see it has all buttons on it!

00:20:56.614 --> 00:21:00.530
So you can really easily attach the fabric to the wood.

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:04.272
I chose to make three pieces, because it seemed easier.

00:21:04.520 --> 00:21:09.939
Also, the velcro was kind of consciously chosen instead of a zipper...

00:21:10.193 --> 00:21:16.018
A zipper might be&nbsp;easier to use,
but I've honestly never installed a zipper...

00:21:16.018 --> 00:21:17.508
And velcro is easier...

00:21:17.508 --> 00:21:22.106
And if something&nbsp;goes wrong with the zipper,
it's very hard to put in a new one.

00:21:22.106 --> 00:21:27.449
But velcro is very easy to just...
to order is cheap, and to sew it in.

00:21:27.449 --> 00:21:31.495
But, of course, you can use a zipper,
 if&nbsp;you're comfortable with doing that.

00:21:31.495 --> 00:21:33.880
So, then this is just a big piece!

00:21:33.880 --> 00:21:38.280
It's like&nbsp;5,5 meters long!

00:21:41.169 --> 00:21:44.417
If I'm correct, it's a semi-flat felled seam.

00:21:44.417 --> 00:21:46.374
It's a waterproof seam!

00:21:46.374 --> 00:21:51.079
You can really easily look up also in YouTube
how to make&nbsp;waterproof seams.

00:21:51.360 --> 00:21:54.029
As you can see, it's a bit too big basically...

00:21:54.029 --> 00:21:57.497
But I did that on purpose,
to have like a&nbsp;bit of an overlap.

00:22:00.204 --> 00:22:02.741
So there is less space for gaps...

00:22:04.080 --> 00:22:10.440
We only have like one button here, 
but I&nbsp;would recommend doing more buttons along the way...

00:22:11.812 --> 00:22:18.180
We added this strap to hold down&nbsp;
the fabric to the wooden structure.

00:22:18.180 --> 00:22:24.019
So the strap is then attached to the base, 
and&nbsp;kind of ties everything together...

00:22:24.019 --> 00:22:27.006
I wanted to make the structure completely out of wood.

00:22:27.006 --> 00:22:33.155
So, I made all of these triangular connections.

00:22:33.775 --> 00:22:38.675
So these basically hold&nbsp;the frame together, 
to give it lateral stability.

00:22:38.675 --> 00:22:44.704
And then these hold the beams in place, 
to give&nbsp;it support in the other direction.

00:22:45.240 --> 00:22:48.745
And yeah, it was nice to kind of try 
and make everything&nbsp;from wood.

00:22:48.745 --> 00:22:50.696
This was wood that I already had...

00:22:52.241 --> 00:22:58.011
We had these removable bolts, so that&nbsp;
everything can be easily taken apart

00:22:58.011 --> 00:22:59.476
But it's a prototype...

00:22:59.476 --> 00:23:03.783
And we wanted to try and come up with&nbsp;something 
with what we had and then something that could be.

00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:12.566
And then, to further secure the frame, 
we&nbsp;bolted it down in four corners to the platform.

00:23:13.186 --> 00:23:15.760
So, then it kind of has four anchoring bolts...

00:23:16.211 --> 00:23:17.406
So, I made&nbsp;a window!

00:23:18.224 --> 00:23:22.717
For extra ventilation, and it's just nice 
to have a see-through, I think....

00:23:23.619 --> 00:23:26.289
You can close&nbsp;it fully, like this...

00:23:27.022 --> 00:23:29.858
It's pretty strong velcro, I have to say...

00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:34.190
This is waterproof, it's a hundred percent cotton!

00:23:34.754 --> 00:23:37.065
I think&nbsp;it's 340 grams...

00:23:37.065 --> 00:23:38.802
Mold resistant!

00:23:39.084 --> 00:23:42.927
Also, when it rains a lot the fibers tend to grow!

00:23:43.153 --> 00:23:47.423
Which&nbsp;makes it extra waterproof.
But then it can also shrink a bit... The fabric.

00:23:48.390 --> 00:23:51.733
So it's also&nbsp;good to keep in mind that it could shrink...

00:23:51.733 --> 00:23:57.720
Especially in length, to make everything
a bit more longer than it's needed, I would say...

00:23:59.340 --> 00:24:00.570
Hello guys!

00:24:00.570 --> 00:24:01.452
- Hello!

00:24:01.452 --> 00:24:03.053
Hello! 
- The tent is done!

00:24:03.053 --> 00:24:04.154
- What do you think?

00:24:04.154 --> 00:24:05.320
This is lovely!

00:24:06.448 --> 00:24:07.630
It's amazing!

00:24:09.540 --> 00:24:11.280
Wow! Love it!

00:24:19.740 --> 00:24:21.933
Now we have our tent prototype!

00:24:21.933 --> 00:24:23.901
We will see how it goes during the season.

00:24:28.260 --> 00:24:34.620
For sure, some people from the Kamp&nbsp;will give it a try, 
and tell us how it is to sleep in this cozy and beautiful space.

00:24:42.498 --> 00:24:46.320
You can get more deep information 
on how to make&nbsp;the tent in the research module.

00:24:46.320 --> 00:24:48.813
Follow the link in the description!

00:24:48.813 --> 00:24:51.282
Next update will be an '8th-number' -video.

00:24:51.282 --> 00:24:53.642
So we will talk about challenges we have...

00:24:53.642 --> 00:24:57.621
And also answer some questions,
that you can&nbsp;ask by commenting on this video.

00:24:57.621 --> 00:25:00.374
You can address them to the different themes of our project...

00:25:00.374 --> 00:25:03.680
Like video making, workspace, landscaping or kitchen.

00:25:03.680 --> 00:25:06.840
Also, you can just ask and we will see who answers!

00:25:07.178 --> 00:25:09.878
Thanks for watching, and see you in the next update!

